config TERMINAL_TYPO_CORRECTOR
	tristate "Terminal Typo Correction support"
	help
	  This module provides automatic typo correction for terminal commands.
	  It uses a simple edit distance algorithm to suggest corrections
	  for commonly mistyped commands.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
	  module will be called typo_corrector.

	  If unsure, say N.

config TERMINAL_ERROR_EXPLAINER
	tristate "Terminal Error Explanation support"
	help
	  This module provides detailed explanations for common kernel errors
	  and system messages. It intercepts kernel messages and adds helpful
	  explanations and fix suggestions.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
	  module will be called error_explainer.

	  If unsure, say N.

config SMART_INPUT
	tristate "Smart Input System support"
	depends on PROC_FS
	help
	  This module provides global smart input features for all Linux
	  applications:
	  - Accent character picker (long-press to see variants)
	  - Smart autocorrect with ghost text + Tab accept
	  - Timestamp converter (Unix → human readable)
	  - Unit converter (km↔miles, kg↔lbs, etc.)
	  - Clipboard history

	  Features are accessible via /proc/smart_input/ and netlink.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
	  module will be called smart_input.

	  If unsure, say N.
